        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore: address gollaw code health audit findings (#293)",
        "body": "## Overview\n\nRefactor to address code health findings from [gollaw](https://github.com/dovocoder/gollaw) static analysis. Closes #293.\n\n## Problem\n\nGollaw v0.2.0-dev identified **762 findings** (health score 0/100, grade F). The most actionable categories were code duplication (89 findings from repeated mutex-guard patterns) and large functions (83 findings with functions exceeding 50 lines).\n\n## Changes\n\n### Extract `lockedClient`/`connectedClient` helpers (`internal/wa/`)\n\nThe `c.mu.Lock(); cli := c.client; c.mu.Unlock(); if cli == nil ...` guard pattern was repeated 46+ times across `client.go`, `groups.go`, `newsletters.go`, `appstate.go`, and `media.go`. Extracted two helpers:\n\n```go\nfunc (c *Client) lockedClient() *whatsmeow.Client  // nil if not initialized\nfunc (c *Client) connectedClient() (*whatsmeow.Client, error)  // error if not connected\n```\n\nEach call site went from 6 lines to 3 lines. **Eliminated 46 duplication findings** (89→43).\n\n### Refactor large functions\n\n| Function | Before | After | Extraction |\n|----------|-------:|------:|------------|\n| `BackfillHistory` | 190 lines | 88 lines | On-demand handler + request loop |\n| `storeParsedMessage` | 169 lines | 67 lines | Contact/group/media/upsert helpers |\n| `extractBusinessText` | 144 lines | <50 lines | Template/buttons/list message handlers |\n| `sendFile` | 159 lines | 71 lines | Media type/proto/persistence helpers |\n\n## Impact\n\n| Metric | Before | After | Δ |\n|--------|-------:|------:|---:|\n| Total findings | 762 | 716 | **−46** |\n| Duplication | 89 | 43 | **−46** |\n| Complexity | 35 | 34 | −1 |\n| Hotspots | 14 | 12 | −2 |\n| Health score | 0/100 (F) | 0/100 (F) | — |\n\nThe health score remains 0/F because deadcode (372, mostly cobra dispatch false positives) and large-functions (83, mostly CLI command constructors) still dominate. These require different approaches (analyzer improvements for cobra, deeper refactoring of command constructors).\n\n## Testing\n\nFull gate passes:\n- `pnpm format:check` ✓\n- `pnpm lint` (go vet) ✓\n- `pnpm test` (go test + FTS5 tests) ✓\n- `pnpm build` (sqlite_fts5) ✓\n- `git diff --check` ✓\n\nNo behavior changes — pure refactoring. All public APIs unchanged.\n",
        "branch": "chore/gollaw-code-health-audit",
